BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Interstellar flight: deep space, ship-time warp</h1>
A delta-glider 2000 AU from the Sun (deep space) accelerates at 1 g for a
year of its own time under a ship-time warp of 10^6: its clock, speed and
distance against hyperbolic motion. Meanwhile the world follows conics:
a vessel in low Earth orbit keeps its orbit over the years. Back in the
Solar System the time acceleration stays within Orbiter's limit.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/InterstellarTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship DS
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET DS
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
DS:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Sun
  ELEMENTS 3.0e14 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 90.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
LEO:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Earth
  ELEMENTS 7.0e6 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 0.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
END_SHIPS
